@startuml authorization-decision
title The authorization decision — where each concept comes into play\n(a pipeline of handlers: every handler runs, except after a suspension)

skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityBorderColor #2688D4
skinparam arrowColor #2688D4
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FCF3D0
skinparam noteBorderColor #C0A040
skinparam partitionBorderColor #A0A0A0

start
:A use case (the **PEP**) asks the **PDP**:
"may **account** A perform **action** X
on **subject account** S?";
note right
  Example: may Jane's account (acc_jane)
  perform **feature.sso.configure**
  in Acme's account (acc_acme)?
end note

:For an employee-initiated use case touching S, **account.read**
on S is checked as a finding of the same decision (AU-4).
The **PIP** (Authorization) loads principal, resource and context;

partition "1 · Account" {
  if (Is A, S (for a feature action or change), or the\n**contact's account** (when a contact asked) suspended?) then (yes)
    if (Terminating action (end, expire, cancel, record)\nor an employee read of S?) then (yes)
      :No Deny finding: the hold is reported
as a fact · the chain continues;
    else (no)
      :Finding: **Deny** · account.<hold>;
      :Decision written to the audit record;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
}

partition "2 · Access — what the actor holds" {
  :Load A's current **roles** in S (fresh, never from the token):
  • **account role assignments** (customers)
  • **birthright role assignments** + internal assignments (employees);
  :Expand roles into **permissions**;
  if (Does A hold the **permission** whose key is X?) then (yes)
    :Finding: Allow · role that grants it;
  else (no)
    :Finding: **Deny** · access.permission-not-held;
  endif
}

partition "3 · Contact access (only when a contact asked)" {
  if (Does the **contact** hold the customer permission in S?) then (yes)
    :Finding: Allow;
  else (no)
    :Finding: **Deny** · access.contact-permission-not-held;
  endif
}

partition "4 · Entitlement — what the subject account has (feature actions)" {
  :S's **subscription** → is it in force?
  → does a **subscription term** cover now? (its plan is the current plan);
  :Effective entitlements = the term's **plan** bundles
  + **add-on** bundles + active **entitlement grants**;
  if (Is the **feature** among them?) then (yes)
    :Finding: Allow · source (plan / add-on / grant), covering term;
  else (no)
    :Finding: **Deny** · entitlement.<reason>;
  endif
}

partition "5 · Policy — requirements on top" {
  :From the active **policy set**, every **policy**
  that governs X and whose **applies_when** holds;
  if (Does every **requires** predicate hold?) then (yes)
    :No policy finding;
  else (no)
    :Finding per unmet policy:
    **Deny**, or **Conditional** with its prerequisites
    (for example, an approval);
  endif
}

:**Decision** = the most restrictive finding
(Deny > Conditional > Allow), with every finding;
:Write the **audit record** (actor, subject,
action, outcome, reason codes); no record, no decision (fail closed);
:The PEP answers per AU-6: **Denied** with reasons only to a
principal holding account.read on S, otherwise **NotFound**;
stop

legend bottom
  **Permission**: the right to perform an action, held through **roles** (Access).
  **Entitlement**: what a subject account can use, from its subscription and **grants** (Entitlement).
  **Grant**: one feature given to one subscription, until an expiry (Entitlement).
  **Policy**: a requirement in positive form; never allows, only constrains (Policy).
  **Subscription term**: which plan, and why it is covered, for a span; nothing works outside a term (Entitlement).
endlegend

@enduml
